# Front-End Dev-Mode: Log-Based Implementation

## Purpose

This file provides specialized guidance for log-based implementation in front-end development. It focuses on using log analysis to diagnose and fix issues, implement new features based on log patterns, and verify implementations through log monitoring.

## Usage as Project-Rule-Parameter

This file contains log-based implementation patterns for front-end development and should be referenced as a project-rule-parameter in message-commands when implementing features through log analysis:

```
dev-mode: front-end-workflow @parameters/front-end/dev-mode/dev-mode-log-based.mdc
```

## Mode Activation

When activated with:

```
dev-mode: front-end-workflow @parameters/front-end/dev-mode/dev-mode-log-based.mdc
```

This parameter enables:
- Log-based analysis and diagnosis
- Log-guided implementation
- Log verification for implementations
- Structured log checking sequences
- Progressive log enhancement

## Implementation Strategy

The log-based implementation strategy follows a structured approach:

### 1. Log Analysis Phase

Begin by analyzing logs to understand current behavior, identify issues, and establish baselines:

```typescript
// 1. Check most recent front-end logs
run_terminal_cmd("Get-Content -Path \"logs-main/front-end/$(Get-Date -Format 'yyyy-MM-dd').log\" -Tail 50", false)

// 2. Check most recent API logs
run_terminal_cmd("Get-Content -Path \"logs-main/api/$(Get-Date -Format 'yyyy-MM-dd').log\" -Tail 50", false)

// 3. Check combined logs for error patterns
run_terminal_cmd("Get-Content -Path \"logs-main/combined/$(Get-Date -Format 'yyyy-MM-dd').log\" -Tail 50 | Select-String -Pattern 'ERROR|WARN|FATAL'", false)

// 4. Search for specific feature logs
run_terminal_cmd("Get-ChildItem -Path \"logs-main\" -Recurse -Filter \"*.log\" | Select-String -Pattern \"[feature-name]\" | Select-Object -Last 20", false)

// 5. Get error logs across all files
run_terminal_cmd("Get-ChildItem -Path \"logs-main\" -Recurse -Filter \"*.log\" | Select-String -Pattern \"ERROR\" | Select-Object -Last 20", false)
```

### 2. Problem Identification Phase

Identify specific issues or requirements based on log analysis:

```typescript
// 1. Identify related components
codebase_search("component related to [log-pattern]", ["front-end/src/components"])

// 2. Locate error source
grep_search("[error-message-from-logs]", false, "*.tsx")

// 3. Understand error context
read_file("[identified-file].tsx", should_read_entire_file=true)

// 4. Examine state handling
grep_search("useState|useReducer|useContext.*[related-state]", false, "*.tsx")

// 5. Check API integration
grep_search("api\\.[method-name]|fetch\\(['\"][endpoint]['\"]", false, "*.tsx")
```

### 3. Implementation Phase

Implement changes based on log analysis findings:

```typescript
// 1. Add logging to component for better visibility
edit_file("front-end/src/components/Feature.tsx", 
          "Add enhanced logging to component",
          "// ... existing code ...\n" +
          "console.log('[Feature] Rendering with props:', props);\n" +
          "// ... existing code ...")

// 2. Fix identified issue
edit_file("front-end/src/components/Feature.tsx", 
          "Fix issue identified in logs",
          "// ... existing code ...\n" +
          "// Fixed error: [description of fix]\n" +
          "// ... updated implementation ...")

// 3. Enhance error handling
edit_file("front-end/src/utils/errorHandling.ts", 
          "Enhance error handling based on logs",
          "// ... existing code ...\n" +
          "// Added better error capture for [scenario]\n" +
          "// ... implementation ...")

// 4. Improve API error management
edit_file("front-end/src/api/apiClient.ts", 
          "Improve API error handling",
          "// ... existing code ...\n" +
          "// Enhanced error handling for API calls\n" +
          "// ... implementation ...")
```

### 4. Log-Enhanced Testing

Create or enhance tests based on log patterns:

```typescript
// 1. Create test for identified scenario
edit_file("front-end/src/components/__tests__/Feature.test.tsx", 
          "Add test for scenario identified in logs",
          "// ... existing code ...\n" +
          "test('should handle [scenario from logs] correctly', () => {\n" +
          "  // Test implementation based on log analysis\n" +
          "});\n" +
          "// ... existing code ...")

// 2. Create error case test
edit_file("front-end/src/utils/__tests__/errorHandling.test.ts", 
          "Add test for error case from logs",
          "// ... existing code ...\n" +
          "test('should handle [error-case] correctly', () => {\n" +
          "  // Test implementation for error scenario\n" +
          "});\n" +
          "// ... existing code ...")
```

### 5. Verification Through Logs

Verify the implementation by checking updated logs:

```typescript
// 1. Request UX situation to generate new logs
console.log("recreate-ux-situation: Please test the fixed feature by [specific steps]")

// 2. Check logs after fix
run_terminal_cmd("Get-Content -Path \"logs-main/front-end/$(Get-Date -Format 'yyyy-MM-dd').log\" -Tail 50", false)

// 3. Verify error is resolved
run_terminal_cmd("Get-ChildItem -Path \"logs-main\" -Recurse -Filter \"*.log\" | Select-String -Pattern \"[previous-error]\" | Select-Object -Last 20", false)

// 4. Validate expected behavior in logs
run_terminal_cmd("Get-ChildItem -Path \"logs-main\" -Recurse -Filter \"*.log\" | Select-String -Pattern \"[expected-success-pattern]\" | Select-Object -Last 20", false)
```

## Common Log Analysis Patterns

### Error Diagnosis Sequence

```typescript
// 1. Find error instances
run_terminal_cmd("Get-ChildItem -Path \"logs-main\" -Recurse -Filter \"*.log\" | Select-String -Pattern \"ERROR\" | Select-Object -Last 20", false)

// 2. Examine error context (lines before/after)
run_terminal_cmd("Get-Content -Path \"logs-main/front-end/$(Get-Date -Format 'yyyy-MM-dd').log\" | Select-Object -First 50 -Skip ([matched-line-number] - 5)", false)

// 3. Track request flow
run_terminal_cmd("Get-Content -Path \"logs-main/combined/$(Get-Date -Format 'yyyy-MM-dd').log\" | Select-String -Pattern \"[request-id]\"", false)

// 4. Check component rendering sequence
run_terminal_cmd("Get-Content -Path \"logs-main/front-end/$(Get-Date -Format 'yyyy-MM-dd').log\" | Select-String -Pattern \"render|mounted|useEffect\"", false)

// 5. Analyze state changes
run_terminal_cmd("Get-Content -Path \"logs-main/front-end/$(Get-Date -Format 'yyyy-MM-dd').log\" | Select-String -Pattern \"state|update|changed\"", false)
```

### API Integration Debugging

```typescript
// 1. Check API requests
run_terminal_cmd("Get-Content -Path \"logs-main/front-end/$(Get-Date -Format 'yyyy-MM-dd').log\" | Select-String -Pattern \"api|fetch|axios|request\"", false)

// 2. Check API responses
run_terminal_cmd("Get-Content -Path \"logs-main/front-end/$(Get-Date -Format 'yyyy-MM-dd').log\" | Select-String -Pattern \"response|received|data\"", false)

// 3. Match requests with backend logs
run_terminal_cmd("Get-Content -Path \"logs-main/api/$(Get-Date -Format 'yyyy-MM-dd').log\" | Select-String -Pattern \"[endpoint]\"", false)

// 4. Check error status codes
run_terminal_cmd("Get-ChildItem -Path \"logs-main\" -Recurse -Filter \"*.log\" | Select-String -Pattern \"status.*4[0-9]{2}|status.*5[0-9]{2}\"", false)

// 5. Examine payload issues
run_terminal_cmd("Get-Content -Path \"logs-main/combined/$(Get-Date -Format 'yyyy-MM-dd').log\" | Select-String -Pattern \"payload|body|data\" -Context 0,5", false)
```

### Performance Analysis

```typescript
// 1. Check rendering times
run_terminal_cmd("Get-Content -Path \"logs-main/front-end/$(Get-Date -Format 'yyyy-MM-dd').log\" | Select-String -Pattern \"render time|rendering took|performance\"", false)

// 2. Identify slow operations
run_terminal_cmd("Get-Content -Path \"logs-main/front-end/$(Get-Date -Format 'yyyy-MM-dd').log\" | Select-String -Pattern \"slow|delay|took [0-9]+ms\" | Sort-Object -Descending { [regex]::Match($_, '\\d+').Value -as [int] }", false)

// 3. Check memory usage patterns
run_terminal_cmd("Get-Content -Path \"logs-main/front-end/$(Get-Date -Format 'yyyy-MM-dd').log\" | Select-String -Pattern \"memory|heap|garbage collection\"", false)

// 4. Analyze component re-renders
run_terminal_cmd("Get-Content -Path \"logs-main/front-end/$(Get-Date -Format 'yyyy-MM-dd').log\" | Select-String -Pattern \"re-render|unnecessary render|render count\"", false)
```

## Common-Usage Scenarios

This parameter is optimized for these common scenarios:

1. **Bug Fixing**: Using logs to diagnose and fix existing issues
2. **Performance Optimization**: Identifying and resolving performance bottlenecks
3. **API Integration Troubleshooting**: Fixing issues with API requests and responses
4. **State Management Debugging**: Resolving issues with component state
5. **User Interaction Problems**: Fixing issues related to user interactions

## Tool Sequence Examples

### Diagnose and Fix Component Error

```typescript
// 1. Check error logs
run_terminal_cmd("Get-ChildItem -Path \"logs-main\" -Recurse -Filter \"*.log\" | Select-String -Pattern \"ERROR.*Component\" | Select-Object -Last 20", false)

// 2. Identify affected component
grep_search("Component.*render|return", false, "*.tsx")

// 3. Examine component implementation
read_file("front-end/src/components/Component.tsx", should_read_entire_file=true)

// 4. Fix the issue
edit_file("front-end/src/components/Component.tsx", 
          "Fix component error identified in logs",
          "// ... existing code ...\n" +
          "// Fixed error: [description]\n" +
          "// ... updated implementation ...")

// 5. Verify the fix
run_terminal_cmd("Get-Content -Path \"logs-main/front-end/$(Get-Date -Format 'yyyy-MM-dd').log\" -Tail 50", false)
```

### Resolve API Integration Issue

```typescript
// 1. Check API error logs
run_terminal_cmd("Get-Content -Path \"logs-main/combined/$(Get-Date -Format 'yyyy-MM-dd').log\" | Select-String -Pattern \"api.*error|fetch.*failed\" -Context 2,2", false)

// 2. Examine API implementation
read_file("front-end/src/api/apiClient.ts", should_read_entire_file=true)

// 3. Check component using the API
grep_search("useEffect.*api\\.[method-name]", false, "*.tsx")

// 4. Fix API integration
edit_file("front-end/src/api/apiClient.ts", 
          "Fix API integration issue",
          "// ... existing code ...\n" +
          "// Fixed API issue: [description]\n" +
          "// ... updated implementation ...")

// 5. Fix component implementation
edit_file("front-end/src/components/Feature.tsx", 
          "Update component to handle API correctly",
          "// ... existing code ...\n" +
          "// Updated API handling: [description]\n" +
          "// ... updated implementation ...")

// 6. Verify with logs
run_terminal_cmd("Get-Content -Path \"logs-main/front-end/$(Get-Date -Format 'yyyy-MM-dd').log\" -Tail 50", false)
```

## Recovery Points

When continuing an interrupted implementation, these recovery points can be used:

1. **Log Analysis Complete**: Logs analyzed, issues identified, ready for implementation
2. **Problem Identified**: Specific issues located in code, ready for fixes
3. **Implementation Started**: Initial changes made, further changes needed
4. **Testing Phase**: Implementation complete, testing in progress
5. **Verification In Progress**: Fixes implemented, verification through logs in progress

